{"actor": "opencode", "data": {"documentation_gaps": {}, "duration_s": 1979.3, "landed_paths": 0, "missing_artifacts": 0, "next": "Land this branch on the shared base with 'tools/origin sync land', then pick up the remaining unclaimed item: the Python equivalent of tests/git-versions.json (defect 6), which docs/operations/vm-execution.md names as unclaimed. T-0030 remains open on instance-20260717-0947; do not start its detector half here.", "outcome": "worked", "push_requested": false, "summary": "T-0031: F, D and T identifiers are now allocated from origin/<base> plus the working tree, and every command that hands out a number prints the record it read. Falsified against the defect's own bytes first: a clone behind the base returned T-0002 where the base already defined it, and a deleted task file recycled its number. The first run also caught two defects in the implementation under test. Two further defects surfaced from running the task's own verification: session start wrote its report before its first event, so doc lint could not pass while a session was open; and cli.py and tasks.py passed the 300-line cap, so the parser and the task template moved to their own modules. 329 tests green; doc lint, release check and preflight exit 0. Ceiling unchanged in kind: two VMs allocating between their own fetches still collide, and T-0030's detector is what catches that.", "unlogged_changes": 12}, "host": "instance-20260717-0944", "kind": "session_end", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 50, "session": "2026-10-04-005-t-0031-allocate-f-d-and-t-identifiers-fr", "ts": "2026-10-04T02:04:00+00:00"}
